				<key>why</key>
				<string>the knee turning one way: its first curve taken into the stem's line (523,496 to 375,166; the stroker had left a curve of 52 units with both handles on its end) and the next curve's handles set one way (362,137 on the line, 350,108 on the upright; was 366,145 and 350,111, an S): two bends at 331,173 and 329,162 upright gone (test_knee_turns_one_way). The redrawn Italic u's knee showed no step, so knee_turned did not run. The entry's first curve the same way (handles 311,633 and 321,653 on the line's and the next curve's directions; was 303,615 and 310,635, a wobble of 9 degrees at 312,634), 0.3 units from where it was. Shape as approved on proofs/2026-11/bold-italic-after-redraw-az-2026-11-11.pdf, within a unit; 2026-11-18 moved 3 right, advance +5, shape untouched: where the run spaces it on the Italic's wider letter (phase 6 step B), so ú ù û, ʉ and Q_u built on it agree; 2026-11-19 moved 0 (advance -1), shape untouched: where the run spaces it on the Italic's letter after phase 6 step C, so what is built on it agrees</string>
